A module of optional values, result values, panic helpers, and byte utilities.

A public record Option of T has a has_value flag as a truth value, and a value as T.

A public record Result of T and E has an is_ok flag as a truth value, an ok_val as T, and an err_val as E.

Publicly, to option_some for T given v as T, returning Option of T.
    Define local value_out as Option of T.
    Set value_out.has_value to true.
    Set value_out.value to v.
    Give back value_out.
Done.

Publicly, to option_none for T, returning Option of T.
    Define local value_out as Option of T.
    Give back value_out.
Done.

Publicly, to option_is_some for T given o as a pointer to Option of T, returning a truth value.
    Give back o.has_value.
Done.

Publicly, to option_unwrap_or for T given o as a pointer to Option of T, fallback as T, returning T.
    If o.has_value:
        Give back o.value.
    Give back fallback.
Done.

Publicly, to result_ok for T and E given v as T, returning Result of T and E.
    Define local value_out as Result of T and E.
    Set value_out.is_ok to true.
    Set value_out.ok_val to v.
    Give back value_out.
Done.

Publicly, to result_err for T and E given e as E, returning Result of T and E.
    Define local value_out as Result of T and E.
    Set value_out.is_ok to false.
    Set value_out.err_val to e.
    Give back value_out.
Done.

Publicly, to result_is_ok for T and E given r as a pointer to Result of T and E, returning a truth value.
    Give back r.is_ok.
Done.

Publicly, to result_unwrap_or for T and E given r as a pointer to Result of T and E, fallback as T, returning T.
    If r.is_ok:
        Give back r.ok_val.
    Give back fallback.
Done.

Publicly, to panic given msg as a pointer to byte, len as an unsigned number, returning nothing.
    Ask Linux kernel 1 with 2, msg, and len.
    Ask Linux kernel 1 with 2, "\n", and 1.
    Ask Linux kernel 60 with 1.
Done.

Publicly, to assert_true given cond as a truth value, msg as a pointer to byte, len as an unsigned number, returning nothing.
    If not cond:
        panic(msg, len).
Done.

Publicly, to mem_zero given dst as a pointer to byte, len as an unsigned number, returning nothing.
    Define local i as an unsigned number.
    While i < len:
        Set item i of dst to 0.
        Add 1 to i.
Done.

Publicly, to mem_eq given a as a pointer to byte, b as a pointer to byte, len as an unsigned number, returning a truth value.
    Define local i as an unsigned number.
    While i < len:
        If a[i] != b[i]:
            Give back false.
        Add 1 to i.
    Give back true.
Done.
